  "description": "The Automatic Evoked Response Detection (ER-Detect) dataset comprises intracranial EEG recordings collected to develop and validate automated methods for detecting evoked responses in clinical neurophysiology. This dataset includes data from patients with epilepsy recorded at Mayo Clinic and University Medical Center Utrecht, providing a resource for advancing computational approaches to identify stimulus-evoked neural activity in invasive electrophysiological recordings. This is a NEMAR-hosted mirror of the OpenNeuro dataset ds004774.",
